  "_readme": "Copy to ~/.claude/toolkit-models.json. Each key under \"agents\" is a shipped toolkit agent name (see plugins/toolkit/agents/*.md). An empty string keeps the model set in that agent's own frontmatter. A value can be any Claude Code model alias (\"sonnet\", \"opus\", \"fable\") or a full model ID such as \"claude-opus-5-5\". \"haiku\" is refused by the toolkit model policy. An explicit per-call model, or CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL_FORCE, always wins over this file. This applies to Agent-tool spawns only, not Workflow scripts (the MR review engine keeps its own model settings).",
